            <ArticleTitle>Haff disease: rhabdomyolysis after eating buffalo fish.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>664-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5811/westjem.2014.6.10.21794</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Haff disease, rhabdomyolysis after ingesting certain types of fish, was first reported in 1924 in Europe. There have been a limited number of cases reported in the United States. We present the case of a patient who presents with symptoms of rhabdomyolysis after eating cooked buffalo fish purchased at a suburban grocery market.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
